hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7921","7967 Amr bin Ali informed us. He said: I am Yahya. He said: I am Sufyan. He said: I am Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Saeed bin Abd. Al-Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the dawn prayer, then he left out a verse, and said: Is Ubayy bin Ka’b among the people? He said: O Messenger of God, have you forgotten such-and-such verse, or has it been abrogated? He said: I forgot it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7922","7968 Muhammad bin Adam bin Sulayman informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Take the Qur’an from four: Ibn Masoud, Ubayy bin Ka’b, and Muadh bin Jabal. And Salim, the servant of Abu Hudhayfah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7923","7969 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I am Affan bin Muslim, he said: I am Wahib, he said: I am Khalid al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Anas The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The most merciful of my nation to my nation is Abu Bakr, the most ardent of them in the matter of God is Omar, and the most truthful in modesty is Othman. The most familiar of them with the Book of God was Ubayy ibn Ka’b, the most knowledgeable of them was Zayd ibn Thabit, and the most knowledgeable of them regarding lawful and unlawful things was Muadh ibn Jabal. Every nation has a trustee. Indeed, the trustee of this nation is Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7924","7970 Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar informed us, saying: Mu’afa bin Imran told us, on the authority of Sulayman bin Bilal, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What an excellent man Abu Bakr, what an excellent man Omar, what an excellent man Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, what a fine man Usayd bin Hudayr, what a fine man Muadh bin Jabal, what a fine man Muadh bin Amr bin Al-Jamouh.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7925","7971 Ahmad bin Saeed informed us. He said: I am Ya’qub bin Ibrahim. He said: I am my father. He said: Yazid bin Al-Had told me that Abdullah bin Khabbab narrated to him, that Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri narrated to him, that Usayd bin Hudair was among us one night reciting in his hall, “When his horse roamed So he recited, then another woman went around and he recited, then she went around again. Usayd said: I was afraid that she would step on Yahya, so I got up to her, and then there was something like a shadow. Above my head, in it were things like lamps. It rose in the air until I could not see it. He said: So I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, yesterday in the middle of the night in my dormitory, my horse galloped, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Read Ibn Hudair, so she recited, then she walked around again, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Ibn Hudair recited, so I recited, and Yahya was close to her. So I was afraid that it would trample on it, so I saw something like a canopy, in which were things like lamps, rising in the air until I could not see them. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: Those angels used to listen to you, and if you had recited, people would have seen them in the morning, but do not hide from them."
"7926","7972 Abu Bakr bin Nafi’ told us, he said: I am Bahz bin Asad, he said: I am Hammad, he said: I am Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that Usayd bin Hudayr And Abbad bin Bishr, “They were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a dark night. Hunnuds went out from him, and a stick lit up.” One of them, so they started walking in its light, and when they separated, the other’s staff lit up.”"
"7927","7973 Abdullah bin Al-Haytham told us, he said: I am Hisham bin Abdul-Malik, he said: I am Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Kinanah bin Nu’aym, on the authority of Abu Barza, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, met the enemy and said: Are you missing anyone? They said: Yes, we are missing.” So-and-so and so-and-so. He said: Are you missing anyone in the second? They said: No. He said: But I am missing a Jalaybib. Go and seek him among the dead. So, behold, he was killed alongside seven people. He killed them, then they killed him. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought and told, and he came until he stood up. He said: This is from me, and I am from him. He killed seven, then they killed him. This is from me, and I am from him. He killed seven, then they killed him. He said it twice, then he carried him on his forearm. He had no bed but he assisted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, until a hole was dug for him and he was buried, but he had none. \"washed\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7928","7974 I am Muhammad bin Al-Ala’, he said: I am Ibn Idris, he said: I heard Shu’bah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “Bring my father He was killed on the day of Uhud, and Fatima made his sister cry for him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not make him cry, the angels are still overshadowing him. with its wings until it was lifted up.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7929","7975 Suleiman bin Salam told us, he said: I am Al-Nadr, he said: I am Hammad, he said: I am Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked forgiveness for me.” May God bless him and grant him peace twenty-five times on the night of the camel."
"7930","7976 Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Al-Aswad bin Shayban told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Samir, he said: Abdul came to us Allah bin Rabah, so I went to him and the Ansar were teaching him jurisprudence, so he said: Abu Qatada Al-Ansari, the knight of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent an army of princes and said: Zaid bin Haritha is upon you. If Zaid is injured, then Ja’far bin Abi Talib If Ja`far was injured, then Abdullah bin Rawaha, then Ja`far jumped up and said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you. I was not afraid that you would attack me. Zaid, and he said: Go ahead, for you do not know what good there is in this. So they set off and stayed as long as God wished, and then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, arrived. He ascended the pulpit and ordered that it be called: Prayer is unified. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not tell you about this invading army of yours? They set off and met the enemy, and Zaid was wounded and became a martyr. They asked for forgiveness for him, and the people asked for forgiveness for him. Then Ja`far ibn Abi Talib took the banner. He oppressed the people until he was killed as a martyr. I gave him martyrdom, so they asked forgiveness for him. Then Major General Abdullah bin Rawaha was taken. So he made his feet firm until he was martyred, and they asked forgiveness for him. Then he took the general, Khalid bin Al-Walid, and he was not one of the princes. He commanded himself. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his two fingers and said: Oh God, it is one of your swords, so he won with it, then he said: Go forth and advance. Your brothers, and let no one disagree, so the people departed in extreme heat, on foot and riding.”"
"7931","7977 Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Muhammad informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Ayan informed us, he said: I am ibn Idris, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays. He said: Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Abdullah bin Rawahah: “If you move the stirrups for us.” He said: I have neglected my statement. Omar said to him: Listen and obey. He said: O God, had it not been for you, we would not have been guided, nor would we have given charity, nor prayed. So send down tranquility upon us and make our feet firm. If we meet, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O God, have mercy on him, and Omar said: It is obligatory. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7932","7978 Ahmad ibn Abi Ubayd Allah informed us, saying: Umar ibn Ali informed us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qays ibn Abi Hazim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rawaha, “He was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on his way, and he said to him: O Ibn Rawaha, come down.” So he moved the stirrups and said: O Messenger of God, I have left that one. Omar said to him: Listen and obey. He said: He threw himself down and said: Oh God, if it were not for We have not been guided, nor have we given charity, nor have we prayed, so send down tranquility upon us, and strengthen our feet when we meet us.”"
"7933","7979 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Abu Mushar, he said: I am Malik, he said: Abu Al-Nadr told me, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad, on the authority of His father, he said: I never heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say to anyone walking on earth: “He is from the people of Paradise, except for Abdullah bin \"Peace\""
"7934","7980 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, on the authority of Yazid bin Amira, said: When death approached Muadh, it was said: “O Abu Abdul-Rahman, Hosanna,” he said: Sit me down. So they sought knowledge with four people: with Uwaimir Abi Al-Darda’, and with Salman, who said: And faith is their place for whomever they seek. He found them, he says it three times, the Persian, and with Abdullah bin Masoud, and with Abdullah bin Salam, who was a Jew. So he converted to Islam, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: He will live with ten people in Paradise.”"
"7935","7981 Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: I am Khalid, he said: I am Praiseworthy, on the authority of Anas, God willing, he said: Abdullah ibn Salam came to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina and said: “I am asking you about three things that only a prophet knows: What are the first signs of the Hour? And the first thing that the people of Paradise will eat is when the child goes to his father and to his mother. He said: Gabriel told me about them earlier, said Abdullah bin. Peace: That is the enemy of the Jews from among the angels. He said: As for the first signs of the Hour, a fire will gather them from the east to the west, and as for The first food that the people of Paradise will eat is the liver of a whale. As for a child, if it precedes the man’s fluid it will be removed, and if it precedes the woman’s fluid I took it off. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but God, and that you are the Messenger of God. He said: O Messenger of God, the Jews are a confused people, even if they knew. By my conversion to Islam, before you asked them about me, they insulted me before you. Then the Jews came and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: What a man, Abdullah. Among you? They said: The best of us, our master, and the son of our master, and the most knowledgeable of us. He said: Did you see if Abdullah bin Salam converted to Islam? They said: May God protect him from Then he went out to them and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. They said: We are evil and the son of evil, so he said: This is what I feared, O Messenger of God.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7936","7982 Muhammad bin Aban informed us, on the authority of Ibn Fudayl, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Khaythamah, on the authority of Qais bin Marwan, on the authority of Omar, he said: The Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever is pleased to read the Qur’an completely as it was revealed, let him read it as Ibn Masoud read.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7937","7983 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abu Muawiyah, he said: I am Al-Amash, and Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, he said: I Musaab bin Al-Miqdam said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Omar, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever likes to read the Qur’an fresh,” and Ishaq said: Fresh as it was revealed, let him read it as Ibn Umm Abd did. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7938","7984 Abu Saleh Al-Makki told us, he said: I am Fudayl and he is Ibn Iyaad, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, and Khaythamah, On the authority of Qais bin Marwan, “A man came to Omar, and Omar said: “Where did you come from? He said: From Iraq, and I left there a man who dictated the Qur’an by heart. He said: Who is he? He said: Ibn Masoud. He said: There is no one among the people more deserving of that than him. Then he said: I will tell you about that: We spent a night with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said the salaam in Abu Bakr’s house, so we went out and heard a man reading in the mosque. He listened, and it was said: A man from the immigrants is praying. He said: Ask. You give him three, then he said: Whoever wants to recite the Qur’an in a complete manner as it was revealed, let him read it as Ibn Umm Abd reads.”"
"7939","7985 Nasr bin Ali informed us, on the authority of Mu`tamar, who is Ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, he said: He told us Ibn Abbas: “Which of the two recitations do you recite? We said: Abdullah’s recitation. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to present the Qur’an in Once every year, and it was presented to him twice in the year in which he was arrested, and Abdullah witnessed what had been abrogated.”"
"7940","7986 Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan and Abdullah bin Muhammad informed us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Stolen. He said: They mentioned Ibn Masoud with Abdullah bin Amr. He said: “I still love him after I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He said: “Recite the Qur’an from four people: Ibn Masoud, Salim the client of Abu Hudhayfah, Ubayy ibn Ka’b, and Muadh ibn Jabal.” Shu'bah said: And Salem, I do not know who the third is, Ubayy or Mu'adh. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7941","7987 Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: I am Yahya bin Adam, he said: I am Qutbah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas said: We were in the house of Abu Musa with a group of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they were looking at a Qur’an, so Abdullah stood up, Abu Masoud said: “I do not know that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, left after him a man more knowledgeable about what God has sent down than this Qa’im.” Abu Musa said “If you say that, he would bear witness when we were absent, and he would be given permission when we were obscured.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7942","7988 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul Wahid told us, he said: I am Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, he said: I am Ibrahim bin Suwayd, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid saying: Ibn Masoud said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “Your permission is upon me to lift the veil. “And to listen to my supplications until I exhaust you.” Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, On the authority of Ibrahim bin Suwayd, on the authority of Abdullah, mursal"
"7943","7989 Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, he said: I am Abdul Rahman, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: “ “I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I see that Abdullah is one of the Ahl al-Bayt.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7944","7990 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saad, “ In this verse: And do not expel those who call upon their Lord in the morning and the evening. He said: It was revealed about six: I, and Ibn Masoud are among them. Then it was revealed: “Give permission to these.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7945","7991 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: I am Yahya, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Abu Ishaq told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, He said: We said to Hudhayfah: “Inform us of a man who is close to the guidance, and is close in sight, and guides the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so that we will meet him.” He said: What “I know of no one whose character, guidance, and guidance are more similar to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the point of being equal to him, than Ibn Umm Abd.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7946","7992 Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: I am Ubayd Allah bin Musa, he said: I am Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we were six people, and the polytheists said: Drive these people away from you, for they are And they are, he said: It was me, Ibn Masoud, a man from Hudhayl, Bilal, and two men whose names I have forgotten, so God Almighty revealed: And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord in the morning and the evening, desiring His face, to His word: the wrongdoers."
"7947","7993 Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Al-Mu’afa told us, he said: I am Al-Qasim, and he is Ibn Ma’n, on the authority of Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir, On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Damrah, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If I had appointed anyone as successor over “Without consulting my nation, I would have appointed Abdullah bin Masoud as their successor.”"
"7948","7994 Muhammad bin Aban told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: I am Al-Awwam, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, and Ahmad bin Sulayman told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun, who said: I am Al-Awwam, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Khaled bin Al-Walid, who said: “There was a talk between me and Ammar. So I spoke harshly to him, and Ammar went off to complain to Khalid to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Khaled and Ammar came to complain. So he began to be harsh to him, and he only increased his harshness, while the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was silent, so Ammar cried and said: O Messenger of God, don’t you see him? He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his head and said: Whoever is hostile to Ammar, God will hate him, and whoever hates Ammar, God will hate him. Khaled said: So I went out, and there was nothing dearer to me than the satisfaction of Ammar, so I met him as I was pleased with him.” The wording is by Ahmad. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7949","7995 Mahmoud bin Ghaylan informed us, he said: I am Abu Dawud, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Salamah, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid. He narrated, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Ashtar, on the authority of Khalid bin Al-Walid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is hostile to Ammar, God will be hostile to him.”"
"7950","7996 Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, he said: Malik bin Ismail told us, he said: Masoud bin Saad told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid. By God, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, on the authority of al-Ashtar, he said: Khalid ibn al-Walid used to force people to pray. After the afternoon prayer, he said: Then Khalid said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me with a expedition, and we struck the people of a household who were alone.” He said Ammar: These people have been detained from us due to their monotheism. I did not pay attention to what Ammar said. Ammar said: I would not have informed the Messenger of God, may God bless him. And when we presented my complaint to him, when he saw that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not defending me, he turned away with tears in his eyes, and the Prophet responded to him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, then he said: O Khaled, do not insult Ammar, for whoever insults Ammar will be reviled by God, and whoever disparages Ammar will disparage him. God, and whoever makes Ammar foolish, God will make him fool. Khalid said: None of my sins are more fearful to me than Ammar making fools. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7951","Ali bin Al-Mundhir informed us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Fudayl, he said: I am Al-Hasan bin Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Shaddad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Al-Ashtar, said: He said: I heard Khalid saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not curse Ammar, for he is one of the Whoever reviles Ammar, God will curse him, and whoever hates Ammar, God will hate him, and whoever despises Ammar, God will despise him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7952","7998 Ishaq bin Mansour informed us, he said: I am Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ammar, on the authority of Amr ibn Sharhabeel, he said: A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke to us. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ammar bin Yasser was filled with"
"7953","7999 Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: I am Muadh, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Amr bin Al-Aas said: “ I hope that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not die on the day he loved a man, and God would admit him to Hell. They said: We used to see him loving you. He may have been using you. He said: God knows best. He loved me or loved me. But we saw him loving a man. They said: Who is that man? He said: Ammar bin Yasser. They said: That is your murderer on the day of Siffin. He said: By God, we killed him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7954","8000 Al-Hussein bin Harith informed us, saying: I am Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Ibn Awn, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Ammar: “The transgressing group will kill you.”"
"7955","8001 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I am Ubayd Allah bin Musa, he said: I am Abdul Aziz bin Siyah, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Aisha, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Ammar was never given a choice between two matters but he chose \"The strongest of them\""
"7956","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub and Ishaq bin Yaqoub bin Ishaq informed us. They said: I am Affan. He said: I am Hammad bin Salamah. He said: I am Thabit. On the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurra, on the authority of Aidh bin Amr, “Salman, Suhayb, and Bilal were sitting, then Abu Sufyan passed by them, and they said: What The swords of God were still taken from the neck of an enemy, so Abu Bakr said: You are saying this to the sheikh of Quraysh. He said: Then he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him, so he told him. He said: O Abu Bakr: You may have angered them. If you had angered them, you have certainly angered your Lord. So he returned. To them, he said: O brothers, perhaps I have angered you. They said: No, Abu Bakr, may God forgive you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7957","8003 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Abu al-Ghaith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “We were sitting at The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: When Surat Al-Jumu’ah was revealed to him, and when he recited: And others of them, when they joined them, he said: Who are these people? Messenger of God, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not consult him until he asked him once, twice, or three times. He said: And among us is Salman, so the Prophet put May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he laid his hand on Salman, then said: If faith were with the Pleiades, men like these would have attained it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7958","8004 Bishr bin Khalid told us, he said: I am Ghandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Recite the Qur’an from four: from Abdullah bin Masoud, and Salem The client of Abu Hudhayfah, Muadh bin Jabal, and Ubayy bin Ka’b.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7959","8005 Abu Saleh Al-Makki told us, he said: I am Fudayl and he is Ibn Iyaad, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, He said: “I still love Ibn Masoud after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, started with it. He said: Take the Qur’an from four people: Ibn Umm Abd And Ubayy bin Ka’b, and Muadh bin Jabal, and Salim, the servant of Abu Hudhayfah.”"
"7960","8006 Muhammad bin Uthman informed us, he said: I am Ibrahim bin Habib bin Al-Shahid, he said: I am my father, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “May God reward you, the Ansar, especially the family of Amr bin Haram, and Sa’d Ibn Ubadah (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7961","8007 Muhammad ibn Hatim ibn Nu’aym informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ali informed me, saying: My father, I did, he said: Abdullah informed us, about the lions. Ibn Shayban, on the authority of Khalid Ibn Samir, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Rabah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ascended The pulpit, so he ordered the caller to call out: Prayer is unified, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The news is confirmed, the news is confirmed, the news is confirmed, isn’t it? Shall I tell you about this invading army of yours? They set out until they met the enemy, but Zaid was wounded and martyred, so they asked forgiveness for him, then he took the banner. Jafar, he became a martyr against the people, and he was killed as a martyr. I bear witness to his martyrdom, so ask forgiveness for him. Then Major General Abdullah bin Rawaha, so he remained firm on his feet until he was injured and became a martyr, so they asked forgiveness for him. Then they took General Khalid bin Al-Walid, who was not one of the princes, so he raised The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, touched his fingers and said: Oh God, it is one of your swords, so be victorious with it. On that day, Khalid was named: the sword of God. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7962","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Wahb bin Zamaa told me, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Saeed bin Yazid, he said: I heard Al-Harith Ibn Yazid Al-Hadrami narrated, on the authority of Ali Ibn Rabah, on the authority of Nashirah Ibn Sumayy Al-Yazani, who said: I heard Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, and he was giving a sermon. The people, so he said: “I apologize to you from Khaled bin Al-Walid, because I ordered him to withhold this money on the double of the immigrants, so he gave him The one of valor, the one of honor, and the one of the tongue. So I removed him and ordered Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, so Abu Amr bin Hafs bin Al-Mughirah said: You removed a sword that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used, and you sheathed a sword that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used, and you set up a banner. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed him, and you had severed ties of kinship and envied the cousin, so Omar said: You are a close relative, young in age. angry at your cousin.”"
"7963","8009 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Mu`tamar told us, he said: I heard Humayd narrating, on the authority of Anas, “that Abu Talha used to throw stones in front of me.” The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, began to look forward, looking at where his arrow fell, and Abu Talha said: Thus O Prophet of God, may you and my mother be sacrificed for my sacrifice without you moving.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7964","8010 Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith told us, he said: We are Abu Salih, he said: I am Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Qubaisa bin Dhu’ayb, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon Abu Salama, and his gaze was torn and his eyes closed. Then he said: O God, forgive Abu Salamah, and raise his rank among the Mahdi, and leave him behind in his descendants among those who will depart, and forgive us and him, O Lord. of the worlds, O God, make his grave spacious for him, and enlighten him in it.”"
"7965","8011 Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub bin Ibrahim informed us, saying: I am Ibn Idris, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Qur’an was recited during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Ubayy, Muadh, Zayd, and Abu Zayd.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7966","8012 Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdul Wahhab Al-Thaqafi, he said: I am Khalid Al-Adha, on the authority of Abu Qalaba On the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The most merciful of my nation to my nation is Abu Bakr, and the strongest of them in the religion of God is Omar. The most knowledgeable of them is Zaid, and the most knowledgeable of them about what is permissible and what is forbidden is Muadh bin Jabal. Indeed, every nation has a trustee, and the trustee of this nation is Abu “Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7967","8013 Al-Haytham ibn Ayyub informed us, he said: I am Ibrahim, he said: I am Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubaid ibn al-Sabbaq, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: “ Abu Bakr sent me a message and said: You are a young, sensible boy. We do not accuse you. You used to write revelations to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then follow the Qur’an and gather it.”"
"7968","8014 Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Abi Shuaib told us, he said: Al-Harith bin Umair told me, He said: I am Ayoub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “He saw as if he had in his hand a piece of brocade, not pointing with it to anything of Paradise except It flew to him, so I told it to Hafsa, so Hafsa told it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Abdullah is a man.” \"good\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7969","8015 Muhammad ibn Al-Muthanna informed us, he said: I am Khalid, he said: Praiseworthy, on the authority of Anas, he said: “Al-Rabi’ broke a running woman’s thanya, so they asked Pardon was granted to them, but they refused, so compensation for damages was offered to them, so they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered retaliation. Anas ibn al-Nadr said: Oh. Messenger of God, break the fold of the spring, and by the One who sent you with the truth, do not break it. He said: O Anas, the book of God is retaliation. The people agreed and pardoned. He said: “Indeed, among the servants of God is he who, if he swore an oath to God, would fulfill it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7970","8016 Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym told us, he said: Habban told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sulayman bin al-Mughirah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas He said: My uncle Anas bin Al-Nadr said: “You were given that name, but you did not witness Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so that was difficult for him, and he said: The first A scene that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, witnessed, and I was absent from it. By God, if God shows me a scene later, God will show me what I will do. He said: He was afraid to say something else, so he testified with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Uhud of the following year, and Saad bin Muadh, and he said: O Abu Amr, where? He said: And the smell of Paradise, I find it rather than anyone else, so he fought until he was killed, and some parts of it were found on his body. And eighty from between, meaning a blow, a throw, and a stab. My aunt Al-Rabi’ bint Al-Nadr, his sister, said: I did not know my brother except by his skin. He said: And this verse was revealed: Among the believers are men who have been true to what they covenanted with God, and among them are those who have died, and among them are those who are waiting. \"And they have not changed anything\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7971","8017 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: I am Khalid, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon Umm Sulaim. So she brought him dates and ghee, and he said: Put your ghee back in his drink, and your dates in his bowl, for I am fasting. Then he got up to a corner of the house. So he prayed a prayer that was not written, and prayed for Umm Sulaim and for her household. Umm Sulaim said: O Messenger of God, I have a special problem. He said: What is it? I said: Your servant Anas, so he did not leave behind anything good in the hereafter or this world without praying for me, then he said: Oh God, grant him wealth and a child and bless him. He said: I am one of the most wealthy Ansar. He said: And my daughter told me that my crucifix was buried when the pilgrims arrived to Basra. “One hundred and twenty-six.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7972","8018 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, he said: I am Ja’far bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Al-Ja’ad Abu Uthman, he said: I am Anas bin Malik, he said: “The Messenger passed by May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Umm Sulaim heard his voice and said: May my father and mother be sacrificed, O Messenger of God, Anis. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed for me. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, three supplications, two of which I have seen, and I hope for the third in the Hereafter.”"
"7973","8019 Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Shaybani. On the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Baraa bin Azib, that he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said on the day of Qurayza to Hassan bin Thabit: “Rebuke the polytheists, for Gabriel is with you.”"
"7974","8020 Ahmad bin Sulaiman informed us, he said: I am Yahya bin Adam, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told Hassan: “Rebuke the polytheists, for the Holy Spirit is with you.”"
"7975","8021 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, “A servant of Hatib came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained to a woodcutter, and he said: O Messenger of God, let a woodcutter enter Hell. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You lied, no. He enters it, for he witnessed Badr and Al-Hudaybiyyah.”"
"7976","8022 Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym told us, he said: Habban told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Thumama bin Abdullah bin Anas He heard Anas say: “When Haram bin Milhan, who was his uncle, was stabbed on the day of Bir Maunah, he said: With blood like this, so he sprinkled it on His face and head, and said: You have won, by the Lord of the Kaaba.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7977","8023 Al-Hussein bin Mansour informed us, he said: I am Al-Hussein bin Muhammad Abu Ahmad, he said: I am Israel bin Yunus, on the authority of Maysara bin Habib On the authority of Al-Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Hudhayfah ibn Al-Yaman, he said: “My mother asked me how long have you known the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? Peace be upon him, so I said to her: Since such-and-such, then she got away from me and cursed me, so I said to her: Leave me alone, for I am coming to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. So I prayed Maghrib with him, and did not leave him until he asked forgiveness for me and you. So I prayed Maghrib with him, and he prayed until the evening prayer, then he turned away and I followed him. Then someone appeared to him, and he took it and left, so I followed him, and he heard my voice, and he said: Who is this? I said: Hudhayfah, and he said: What’s the matter with you? So I spoke to him. regarding the matter, and he said: May God forgive you and your mother. Did you not see the symptom that was presented to me before? I said: Yes, he said: He is one of the angels who did not He had never descended to earth before this night. He asked permission from his Lord to greet me, and gave me good tidings that Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein were the masters of the youth. The people of Paradise, and that Fatima is the mistress of the women of the people of Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7978","8024 Ahmad ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: I am poor ibn Bukayr, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: “ I came to the Levant, entered the Damascus Mosque, prayed two rak’ahs, then said: Oh God, grant me a good companion. So I sat next to Abu Darda’, and he said to me: “Who are you from?” I said: “From the people of Iraq.” He said: How did Abdullah recite: “And the night when it covers {1} and the day when it becomes clear” {2} And He did not create the male and the female. {3} I said: This is how Abdullah used to recite it. Abu Al-Darda’ said: This is how I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. Then he said: Among you is the one who was protected from Satan: Ammar bin Yasser, and among you is the one who knows the secret that no one else knows, meaning Hudhayfah bin “Al-Yaman”"
"7979","8025 Abu Dawud told us, he said: I am Affan, he said: I am Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sons of Al-Aas are believers: Hisham and Amr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7980","8026 Muhammad bin Hatim informed us, he said: I am Habban, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Musa bin Ali bin Rabah, he said: I heard my father, saying: I heard Amr ibn Al-Aas saying: “The people in Medina were terrified with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they dispersed. I saw Salim hiding his sword, so he sat in the The mosque. When I saw that, I did the same as he did. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out and saw me safe and sound, and he came to the people and said: O people, is your concern before God and His Messenger, is that you did not do what these two believing men did? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7981","8027 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Jarir, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not see me.” He, peace and blessings be upon him, smiled in my face and said: From this door will enter upon you one of the best of Yemen, on his face the face of a king.”"
"7982","8028 Musa bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Jarir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me May God bless him and grant him peace: “Will you not relieve me of Dhul-Khalasa?” I said: Yes, so I set off with one hundred and fifty horsemen from Ahmose, who were owners of horses, so I was I do not ride horses, so I mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he struck his hand on my chest and said: Oh God, steady him and make him a guide. Mahdi, he said: I have never shunned a horse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7983","8029 Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Ghazwan, Al-Hussein bin Harith informed us, saying: I am Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, On the authority of Mugheerah ibn Shubayl, on the authority of Jarir ibn Abdullah, he said: “When I came to Medina, I set my camels, removed my robes, and put on my robes. I entered while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was addressing the people. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted me. The people stared at me, so I said: To my companion: That is, Abdullah, did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mention anything about my matter? He said: Yes, so he spoke well. He said: While he was there? He was giving a sermon when he presented his sermon and said: A man will enter upon you from this door, from this dawn, from the best of Yemen. And on his face was the expression of an angel. He said: “So I thanked God for what He had given me.” The wording is from Muhammad. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7984","8030 Amr bin Ali informed us, he said: I am Yahya, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “A righteous man died: Asahma, so stand up and pray for him, so we stand up and pray for him.”"
"7985","8031 Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: I am Ismail, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra, he said: Ashjaj Bani Asr: he said to me The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, there are two characteristics in you that God loves. I said: What are they? He said: Forbearance and modesty. I said: ancient or modern.” He said: Rather, in the past, I said: Praise be to God who created me with two creatures that God loves."
"7986","8032 Ahmad bin Saeed told us, he said: I am Wahb bin Jarir, he said: Qurrah told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurrah, on the authority of his father, he said: “ I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I asked him for permission to insert my hand, so he touched the ring. He said: So I inserted my hand into his sock, and he is praying. What prevented him, when I touched him and prayed for me, he said: I found on the lower part of his shoulder like a piece of silver, the seal of the Prophethood. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7987","8033 Muhammad bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Khalid, who is Ibn Al-Harith, who said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Dhakwan, on the authority of Ubayy. Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not curse my companions, for if one of you were to spend as much as Uhud in gold, it would not reach a mudd. “One of them, not even half of them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7988","Hafs bin Omar told us, he said: I am Hussein bin Ali, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Do not curse my companions, for if one of you were to spend as much as Uhud in gold, it would not amount to a mudd or half of any of them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7989","8035 Al-Hussein bin Mansour bin Jaafar told us, he said: Mubashir bin Abdullah told us, he said: I am Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Ali bin Muslim, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, who said: Ibn Abbas said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in Mecca, and Abu Bakr and Omar, The companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, were immigrants, because they abandoned the polytheists, and the Ansar were immigrants, because Medina was A trap took place, so they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the night of Aqaba.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7990","8036 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Khaled, he said: I am Praiseworthy. He said: Anas said: “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, loved to The Muhajireen will follow him, and the Ansar will follow him, to take from him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7991","8037 Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: I am Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Sa’d, he said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace in the ditch, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O God, there is no life except the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Muhajireen and the Ansar."
"7992","8038 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadr told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Abu Iyas told us, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, the good is the best of the Hereafter, so make good the Ansar and the Emigrants.”"
"7993","8039 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of An-Nadr, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “O God, the best is the best of the Hereafter, forgive the Ansar and the Emigrants.”"
"7994","8040 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: Anas told us, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us And peace be upon him. He said in the hadith: “Honor the Ansar and the Muhajira.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7995","8041 Ahmad bin Sulaiman informed us, he said: I am Miskin bin Bukayr, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Humaid al-Tawil, on the authority of Anas, he said: “It was The Ansar said on the Day of the Trench: “We are the ones who pledged allegiance to Muhammad for jihad as long as we live.” The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, answered them: Oh God, there is no life except the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7996","8042 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: I am Hamid, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out on a cold morning. And the Muhajireen and the Ansar were digging the trench, so he said: O God, the good is the best of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajira, so they answered him: We are the ones who pledged allegiance to Muhammad to wage jihad as long as we live forever.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7997","8043 Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Abdul-Aziz told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: “Around Medina, and they They tremble and move dust on their bodies, and say: We are the ones who pledged allegiance to Muhammad for Islam as long as we remain. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he, peace and blessings be upon him, answered them: Oh God, there is no good except the good of the Hereafter, so bless the Ansar and the Emigrants. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7998","8044 Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, he said: I am Muhammad, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Perhaps Abu al-Qasim, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If the Ansar had taken a valley, or a path and the people had taken a valley, Or a people, I would have taken Wadi al-Ansar, and had it not been for the migration, I would have been one of the Ansar. Abu Hurairah said: He did not wrong my father and my mother. They sheltered him and supported him, and another word.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"7999","8045 Amr ibn Sawad ibn al-Aswad ibn Amr informed us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas He said: “When the immigrants from Mecca came to Medina, they came with nothing in their hands, and the Ansar were the people of land and property, so he divided among them The Ansar provided that they gave them half of the fruits of their wealth every year, and provided them with work and provisions. His mother was Umm Anas, and she was called Umm Sulaym. Umm Abdullah bin Abi Talha was Anas’s maternal brother. Umm Sulaym gave to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Ibn Shihab said: Then Anas Ibn Malik: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished killing the people of Khaybar and left for Medina, he returned the immigrants to the Ansar. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, returned to Umm Anas the best of them, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave He gave Umm Ayman her place.”"
"8000","8046 Ahmad bin Hafs told us, he said: It is my father, he said: Abraham told me, on the authority of Moses, he said: Abu al-Zinad told me, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Ansar said: “O Messenger of God, O Messenger of God, divide the palm trees between us and our brothers,” and he said: Yes, He said: You are sufficient for us in the provision, and we will share with you in the fruits. They said: We hear and we obey."
"8001","8047 Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: I am Ismail, he said: Praiseworthy narrated to us, on the authority of Anas, he said: “Abd al-Rahman bin Awf came to us, So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a brotherhood between him and Saad bin Al-Rabi’, who was one of the most wealthy of them. Saad said: The Ansar have learned. I am one of the richest of her, so I will divide my wealth between you and me in two parts, and I have two wives, so see which one of them likes you, and I will divorce her. I married her, and Abd al-Rahman said: May God bless your family. Show me the market. He did not return that day even with the best ghee. \"And I drop\""
"8002","8048 Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, saying: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “The Ansar do not hate a man who believes in God and the Last Day,” and he said: “If it had not been for the migration, I would have been a man of the Ansar, even if I had followed the path of “The Ansar is a valley and a people. I would have walked through their valley and their people. The Ansar are my banner, and the people are my covering.”"
"8003","8049 Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Harami bin Amara told me, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Usayd bin Hudayr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Ansar are my honor and my defect. People will increase and decrease, so accept from their doers of good.” And they turned away from their transgressors.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8004","8050 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna informed us, he said: I am Muhammad, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Qatada, speaking on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Ansar are my honor and my defect, and the people will increase and decrease, so accept from their doers of good. And they turned away from their transgressors.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8005","8051 Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Ismail, he said: Praiseworthy, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And who My life is in His hand. If the people took a valley and the Ansar took a valley, I would take the people of the Ansar. The Ansar are my throne and my defect. Migration, I would have been one of the Ansar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8006","8052 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abu Al-Walid, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Anas bin Malik, He says: The Ansar said on the day of the conquest of Mecca: “Our swords are dripping with the blood of Quraysh, and they are taking away the spoils in particular.” So he said: What Did he inform me about you? And they were not lying. They said: He is the one who informed you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Are you not satisfied that he should go? These people are taking the spoils to their homes, and you are taking the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to your homes. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said? And he said: If the Ansar had taken a valley or a path, I would have taken the Ansar’s valley or a path."
"8007","8053 Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Ismail, he said: I am Praiseworthy, on the authority of Anas, “that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out one difficult day.” His head, and the descendants of the Ansar and their servants met him with the faces of the Ansar, saying: By the One in whose hand is my soul, I love you, twice. Or three, then he said: The Ansar have fulfilled what was against them, and what is against you remains, so do good to their doers of good, and turn away from their wrongdoers. \" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8008","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Hisham bin Zayd, on the authority of Anas, “that a woman came to him And with her was a boy of hers whom she was talking to. He said, “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, you are the most beloved people to me.” Three times, as if he meant himself. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8009","Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, he said: I am Ibn Idris, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Hisham bin Zayd bin Anas, on the authority of his grandfather Anas, he said: “ An Ansar woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, you are among the most beloved people to me. “Whoever loves them will love them because of me, and whoever hates them will hate them because of him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8010","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Jabr, he said: I heard Anas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sign of the hypocrite is his hatred of the Ansar, and the sign of the believer is his love of the Ansar.”"
"8011","Ahmad bin Suleiman told us, he said: I am Yazid bin Harun, he said: I am Yahya bin Saeed, that Saad bin Ibrahim informed him about the ruling. bin Mina, that Yazid bin Jariyah told him that Muawiyah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever loves... God loves the Ansar, and whoever hates the Ansar, God hates him.”"
"8012","Muhammad bin Adam bin Sulaiman and Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Ansar do not hate a man who believes in God and the Last Day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8013","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna informed us, saying: I am Muadh bin Muadh, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said regarding the Ansar: “No one loves them except a believer, and no one hates them except an unbeliever. Whoever loves them, God will love him, and whoever Whoever hates them, God hates him.” Shu’bah said: I said to Adi: Did you hear this from Al-Bara’? He said: It happened to me (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8014","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: I am my uncle, he said: I am my father, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, who said: Anas bin Malik told me that he said: “When God gave back to His Messenger what he had given of Hawazin’s wealth, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He gave a man from the Quraysh one hundred camels, and a man from the Ansar said: May God forgive the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He gives Quraysh, and he is leaving us, and our swords are dripping with their blood. Anas said: This was reported to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he sent for the Ansar. So he gathered them in a dome made of human flesh, and did not leave anyone with them. When they gathered, he said: What hadith has reached me on the authority of you? The Ansar jurists said: Either Those of us who have an opinion did not say anything. Rather, there were people whose teeth were fresh, so they said: May God forgive the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he will give Quraysh, and he left us, and our swords were dripping with their blood, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I will give men, the hadith of their covenant. Of disbelief, so I befriend them. Would you not be satisfied for the people to go with the money, and for you to return to your camps with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? By God, what you are faced with is better than what they are faced with. They said: Yes, O Messenger of God, we are satisfied. So he said to them: You will meet After me there will be a severe impact, so be patient until you meet Allah and His Messenger at the Fountain. Anas said: But we were not patient."
"8015","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, that he heard Anas bin Malik say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Shall I not inform you of the best of the Ansar’s homes, or the best of the Ansar?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Banu al-Najjar, then those who They are followed by Banu Abd Al-Ashhal, then those next to them are Banu Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj, then those next to them are Banu Sa’idah, then he said With his hand, he clenched his fingers, then spread them out like an archer with his hands, then he said: The homes of the Ansar are all good."
"8016","Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali told us, he said: Ishaq bin Issa told us, he said: I am Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, that he heard Anas bin Malik says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not inform you of the best of the Ansar’s homes? Banu al-Najjar, then Banu Abd.” Al-Ashhal, then Balharith bin Al-Khazraj, then Banu Sa’idah, said: And in all the homes of the Ansar, all of them are good.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8017","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Ismail, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Shall I not inform you of something good? The house of the Ansar? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: The house of Banu al-Najjar, then the house of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then the house of Balharith ibn al-Khazraj. Then there was the dwelling of Banu Sa`idah, and in every dwelling of the Ansar there was good.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8018","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ja`far, on the authority of Shu`bah, he said: I heard Qatada speaking, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Usayd, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best houses of the Ansar were Banu al-Najjar, then Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu al-Harith bin Khazraj. Then Banu Sa`idah, and there was good in every town of the Ansar. Sa`d said: I did not see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except that he had given favor to us. It was said: He had He has favored you over many.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8019","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: I am Abu Dawud, he said: I am Harb bin Shaddad, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Abu Salamah told me, Abu Usayd Al-Ansari told him that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The best of the Ansar, or the best of the houses of the Ansar, are Banu al-Najjar.” Then Banu Abd Al-Ashhal, then Banu Al-Harith, then Banu Sa’idah.”"
"8020","Ahmad ibn Harb told us, he said: I am Qasim, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Usayd, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The best of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar, then Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then Banu Abd al-Harith bin al-Khazraj, then Banu “Help, and all is well.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8021","Abu Dawud told us, he said: I am Ya’qub bin Ibrahim, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, that Abu Salamah told him, He heard Abu Usayd testify that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best homes of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar, then Banu Abd.” Al-Ashhal, then Banu Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj, then Banu Sa’idah.”"
"8022","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, my uncle told me, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: He said: Abu Salamah and Ubayd Allah, I heard Abu Hurairah, who was in a large gathering of Muslims, inform you about the best of the Ansar’s homes? They said: Yes. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Bani Abd al-Ashhal.” They said: “Then who, O Messenger of God?” He said: “Then Bani al-Najjar.” They said: Then who, O Messenger of God? He said: Then Bani Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj. They said: Then who, O Messenger of God? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: Banu Sa`idah. They said: Then who, O Messenger of God, said: There is good in every town of the Ansar?"
"8023","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, he said: I am Khalid, he said: I am Shu`bah, on the authority of Qatada, he said: I heard Anas speaking, on the authority of Usayd ibn Hudayr, “A man from the Ansar came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Will you not use me as you used so-and-so?” He said: You After me you will meet a trail, so be patient until you meet me at the basin.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8024","Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: I am Asim bin Suwayd bin Amir bin Zaid bin Jariyah, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Anas bin Malik He said: “Usayd ibn Hudayr al-Ashhali, the captain, came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he had distributed food, and the people of a household from The Banu Zafar of the Ansar were in need, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: O master, you have left us until what is in our hands is gone. So if you hear of something that has come to us, then mention to me the people of that house. He said: After that, food came to him from Khaybar: barley and dates. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, swore among the people, and he swore among the Ansar, and he swore extensively, and he swore among the people of that house, and Usayd ibn Hudair said to him: May God reward you, that is, the Prophet of God, with the best reward, or he said: well. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And you are the Ansar. So may God reward you with the best reward, or he said: good, for I have not known anyone to be chaste and patient, and after me you will see an impact in the matter and the oath, and be patient. Until you throw me at the basin.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8025","8071 Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Marwazi told us, he said: Shazan bin Othman told us, he said: Ubayy told us, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Hisham bin Zayd, He said: I heard Anas bin Malik say: “Abu Bakr passed by one of the Ansar’s gatherings and they were crying, so he said: What makes you cry? They said: We mentioned the meeting of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from us, so he entered upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him of that, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out. May God bless him and grant him peace. So he ascended the pulpit, and he did not ascend it after that day. He thanked God and praised Him, then he said: I advise you By the Ansar, for they are my honor and my defect, and they have fulfilled what was due to them, and what remains is what is theirs, so accept from their doers of good, and they have neglected \"Their abuser\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8026","8072 Ali bin Hajar informed us, saying: I am Ismail, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O people Ansar, did I not come to you while you were misguided, and God guided you through me? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Did I not come to you while you were enemies? Between you and me? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Will you not say: Did you not come to us in fear and we made you safe? You were expelled and we sheltered you, and you were deserted and we helped you? The Ansar said: Rather, the manna belongs to Allah and His Messenger. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8027","8073 Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: I am Hamid, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, walked To Badr, he consulted the Muslims, and Abu Bakr advised him, then he consulted them, and Omar advised him, so the Ansar said: O people Ansar, beware of you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wants to say: Then we will not say what the Children of Israel said to Moses: So go, you and your Lord. So fight, and by the One who sent you with the truth, if you had brought their hearts to the pools of darkness, we would have followed you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8028","8074 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: I am Ja’far, meaning Ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He visited the Ansar, greeted their children, stroked their heads, and prayed for them.”"
"8029","8075 Amr bin Ali informed us, he said: I am Yazid bin Zuray’, he said: I am Sa’id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “O God, forgive the Ansar, their children, and their children’s children.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8030","8076 Imran bin Bakkar informed us, saying: I am Abu Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Safwan, on the authority of Shuraih, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Aidh al-Azdi, On the authority of Amr bin Abasa Al-Salami, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Most of the tribes in Paradise are slaughtered.”"
"8031","8077 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Khaled, he said: I am Praiseworthy, he said: Anas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He presents Over you are people who are softer in heart than you. He said: Then the Ash’arites came, including Abu Musa. When they came from Medina, they began to tremble: “Tomorrow.” We meet our beloved ones, Muhammad and his party.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8032","8078 Amr bin Ali informed us, he said: I am Yahya, he said: I am Shu’bah, he said: I am Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Murrah, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Many of the men were perfect, but none of the women were perfect, except for Maryam, daughter of Imran, and Asiya, Pharaoh’s wife.” \""
"8033","8079 Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: I am Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jaafar, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best of her women is Maryam bint Imran, and the best of her women is Khadija.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8034","8080 Al-Abbas bin Muhammad told us, he said: I am Yunus, he said: Dawud bin Abi Al-Furat told us, on the authority of Alba, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best women of the people of Paradise are Khadija bint Khuwaylid and Fatima bint Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And peace be upon him, and Maryam bint Imran, and Asiyah bint Muzahim, Pharaoh’s wife.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8035","8081 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, he said: I am Ghandar, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Murrah al-Hamdani, on the authority of Abu Musa On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Many of the men completed it, but none of the women completed it, except for Maryam bint Imran and Aasiya bint Muzahim.” Pharaoh's wife (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8036","8082 Ibrahim bin Yaqoub informed us, he said: I am Abu Al-Numan, he said: I am Dawud bin Abi Al-Furat, on the authority of Alba bin Ahmar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drew four lines on the ground, then said: Do you know what this is? They said: God and His Messenger know best, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best women of the people of Paradise are: Khadija bint Khuwaylid and Fatima. The daughter of Muhammad, Maryam the daughter of Imran, and Asiyah the daughter of Muzahim, Pharaoh’s wife.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8037","8083 Amr bin Ali informed us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Fudayl, he said: I am Amara, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he heard him say: “He came Gabriel the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Convey blessings from God and my peace to Khadija, and give her good tidings of a house in Paradise made of reeds, in which there will be no noise. And we do not put it in the accusative case. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8038","8084 Ahmad bin Fadalah bin Ibrahim told us, he said: It is Abd al-Razzaq, he said: It is Ja’far bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: “Gabriel came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Khadija was with him. He said: God extends his greetings to Khadija, and she said: Indeed, God is peace. And peace be upon Gabriel, and may God’s peace, mercy, and blessings be upon you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8039","8085 Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave Khadija good news of a house in Paradise, in which there will be no noise and no hardship.”"
"8040","8086 Suleiman bin Salam told us, he said: I am Al-Nadr, he said: I am Hisham, he said: my father told me, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: “I was not jealous.” For the wife of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, just as I was jealous for Khadija, because of the frequent mention of her by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he praised her, and it was revealed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to give her good tidings of a home in Paradise.”"
"8041","8087 Al-Hussein bin Harith informed us, saying: I am Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “What I envied a woman who did not envy Khadija, and he did not marry me until after she died. This is because the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave her good news of a house in... Paradise, there is no noise or hardship.”"
"8042","8088 Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, he said: I am Hamid and he is Ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha said: “I have never been more jealous of a woman than I am of Khadija, because of the frequent mention of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to her.” She said: He married me three years later.”"
"8043","8089 Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Minhal, he said: Dawud bin Abi Al-Furat told us, on the authority of Alba, on the authority of Ikrimah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drew lines on the ground. He said: Do you know what this is? They said: God and His Messenger know best.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best women of the people of Paradise are Khadija bint Khuwaylid and Fatima bint Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. And Maryam bint Imran, and Asiyah bint Muzahim, Pharaoh’s wife.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8044","8090 Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, he said: Zayd bin Hubab told me, he said: Israel bin Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told me, On the authority of Maysarah bin Habib Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr Al-Asadi, on the authority of Zirr bin Hubaysh, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he is Ibn Al-Yaman, “that His mother said to him: When did you make a covenant with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: I have not had a covenant with him since so and so, so she decided to get rid of me. So I said: Leave me alone, for I will go and will not leave him until he asks forgiveness for me and he asks forgiveness for you. I prayed Maghrib with him, then he stood up and prayed until he prayed. Dinner, then he went out and I went out with him, and suddenly someone came to him, then he went and saw me, and said: Hudhayfah, so I said: At your service, the Messenger of God Did you see the model who was shown to me? I said: Yes. He said: He is one of the angels who asked his Lord for permission to greet me and give me good tidings of the arrival of good news. “Al-Hussein is the master of the youth of Paradise, and Fatima, the daughter of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the mistress of the women of the people of Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8045","8091 Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, he said: I am Abdul Wahhab, he said: I am Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “Sickness The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then Fatima came and mourned for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He comforted her and she wept, then she mourned. He pleased her, and she laughed. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, I asked her, and she said: When I leaned on him, he told me that he was dead. Because of the pain that caused him, I cried, then I leaned on him and he told me that I was the fastest to catch up with his family, and that I was the mistress of the women of the people of Paradise. Except for Maryam bint Imran, so I raised my head and laughed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8046","8092 Muhammad bin Rafi’ told me, he said: I am Suleiman bin Dawud, he said: I am Abraham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called his daughter Fatima during the pain in which he died, so he comforted her with something and she cried. Then he called her and comforted her. She laughed and said: So I asked her about that, and she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me that he was suffering from this pain. I cried, then he told me that I was the first of his family to join him, and I laughed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8047","8093 Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: I am Sa’dan bin Yahya, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha She said: “The wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gathered, and not one of them left.” She said: Then Fatima came, walking as if her walk was The walk of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Welcome to my daughter. Then he sat her down and walked over to her. She spoke recently and she cried, so I said when she cried: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, singled you out for his speech rather than us. Then you cried. Then he confided to her a speech. She laughed, and I said: I have never seen joy closer to sadness than today. So I asked her about what he told her, and she said: I would not reveal a secret. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he died, I asked her, and she said: He had spoken to me. He said: Gabriel used to visit me once every year. He came to me twice this year, and I do not see me unless my time has come, and you are the first of my family to join me, and what an excellent predecessor I am to you, so I cried, then It pleased me: Aren’t you satisfied with being the leader of the women of the believers, or the women of this nation? She said: She laughed at that. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8048","8094 Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, he said: I am Uthman bin Omar, he said: I am Israel, on the authority of Maysara bin Habib, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, On the authority of Aisha bint Talha, that Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, said: “I have never seen anyone more like his character, guidance, and closeness to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when she was standing and sitting with Fatima, daughter of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. She said: Whenever she entered upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up to her, kissed her, and made her sit in his seat. Whenever the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon her, she would stand up. Her sitting, so she kissed him and made him sit in her sitting. When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, fell ill, Fatima entered and leaned over him. She kissed him, then raised her head and wept, then leaned on him, then raised her head and laughed, so I said: If I were to think that This is one of the wisest women, so she is one of the women. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, I said: Did you see when you became sad for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? So you raised your head and cried, then you bowed down to him and you raised your head and laughed. What made you do that? She said: Tell me what you mean? He died from this pain, so I cried, then he told me that I was rushing my family to catch up with him, and that is when I laughed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8049","8095 Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaykah, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “As for Fatima, she is a part of me. Whoever dislikes her dislikes me, and whoever harms her harms me.”"
"8050","8096 Al-Harith bin Miskin, it was read to him, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fatima is a part of me. Whoever makes her angry makes me angry.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8051","8097 Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad informed us, he said: I am my uncle, he said: I am my father, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Halhala, that he narrated to him, that Ibn Shihab narrated to him, that Ali bin Hussein narrated to him, that Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, said: “ I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivering a sermon, while I was in a wet dream on that day: “Fatima is from me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8052","8098 Imran bin Bakkar told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Abu Al-Zannad told me, from what Abdul Rahman told him Al-Araj, from what he mentioned, is that he heard Abu Hurairah, speaking on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Abraham migrated to Sarah, and entered In it is a village in which there is a king of kings, or a mighty man of the mighty. It was said: Abraham entered that night with a woman, the best of women. So he sent to him saying: O Abraham, who is this woman with you? He said: My sister. Then he returned to her and said: Do not lie to me, I have told them that it is you. My sister, by God, there is a believer on earth besides me and you, so he sent a message to him to send her, so he sent her to him, so he stood up to her, and she stood up. He performed ablution and prayed, and she said: O God, if I believe in you and your messenger, and guard my chastity except over my husband, do not force this infidel over me. Then he sank down until he ran with his foot.” Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Salamah said: Abu Hurairah said: She said: Oh God, if he died, he would say: She She killed him. “So he was sent the second, and the third, and said: By God, you have not sent to me except a devil. Return to Abraham and give her He emigrated and returned to Abraham, and she said: Do you feel that God suppressed the infidel and served a female child?"
"8053","8099 Wasil bin Abdul-Ala informed us, saying: I am Abu Usama, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, Abraham did not lie except three times, about God, his saying: I am sick, and his saying: Rather, the eldest of them did this. He said: While he was walking in the land of one of the giants, he camped at a certain place, and a man came to the giant, and he said: A man has settled here in your land with a woman from the best of people. He sent to him and said: Who is this woman of yours? He said: She My sister. He said: Go and send for her. He said: So he went to Sarah and said to her: This tyrant asked me about you, so I told him: You are my sister, so do not deny me in his presence, for you are my sister in the Book of God Almighty, and there is no Muslim on earth except me and you. So he set off with her and stood up. Ibrahim was praying, and when she came to him and he saw her, he fell in love with her, so he took her, and he was seized with something similar to her. He was greatly distressed, and said: Pray to God for me. And I will not harm you. So she prayed for him and he sent, so he liked it and took it, so he took something similar to it, or worse than it, then he did that a third time. Then he was taken and mentioned the same as the first two times, and he stopped and said: Pray to God for me and I will not harm you. So she prayed for him and he was sent, then he called for the lowest of his hijab. He said: You did not bring me a human being, but you brought me a devil. Cast her out and give Hagar. He said: So I went out and gave Hagar. So she came, and when Abraham felt her coming, he left his prayer and said: Muhayyim. So she said: God has sufficed the plot of the infidel, and Hagar has served me. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8054","8100 Suleiman bin Salam told us, he said: I am Al-Nadr, he said: I am Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “He did not lie.” Abraham, peace be upon him, never told anything, except for three lies: two about the essence of God: Then he looked at the stars {88} and said, “Indeed, I am sick” {89}, and his saying in Surat Al-Anbiya: He said, “Rather, this is what the eldest of them did.” He said: He came to one of the kings, and with him was a woman, and he asked him about her. So he told him that she was his sister. He said: Tell her: Come to me, or tell her to come to me. So he came to her and said to her: This is what he asked of me. About you, and I told him that you are my sister, and that you are my sister in the Book of God Almighty, and that there is not a believing man or believing woman on earth except me and you. And he has commanded you to come to him. He said: So she came. He looked at her and pressed him and said: Pray for me and for you so that I do not return. He said: So let him go. So he returned, he said: Then he pressed the same way, or more strongly, and said: Pray for me, and that I may not return. He said: So he left him, so he ordered food for her. He served her as a slave girl, called Hagar. When she came to Abraham, he said: Muhayyim, and she said: May God suffice the plot of the immoral infidel, and he served A slave girl. Abu Hurairah said: That is your mother, O sons of the waters of the sky, and Ibn Aoun extended his voice to her."
"8055","8101 Ahmad bin Saeed informed us, he said: I am Wahb bin Jarir, he said: I am my father, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, On the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “When Gabriel ran over Zamzam, he pushed his heel and water spewed out, so Hagar started gathering The bath around the water so that it does not disperse. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God have mercy on Hagar. If she had left it, it would have been a spring. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8056","8102 Abu Dawud told us, he said: I am Ali bin Al-Madini, he said: I am Wahb bin Jarir, he said: my father told us, he said: I heard Ayyub narrating, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Gabriel descended to Hagar, And Ismail, so he ran over the place of Zamzam with his heel, and water spewed out. He said: So Hagar made the bathtubs gather around him so that the water would not disperse. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God have mercy on Hagar, if she had left her, he would have been a helper. He said: So I said to Abu Hammad: He does not mention Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and he does not raise it. He said: I memorized it like this. Ayoub told me about it. Wahb said, and Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub, On the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and the like, but he did not mention my father, nor the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Wahb said: So I went to Salam bin Abi Muti’, and he told me this hadith, and it was narrated to him on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Saeed Ibn Jubayr, and he responded strongly to that, then he said to me: What does your father say? I said, “My father.” He says: Ayoub, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, said: It is amazing, by God, that the man from among our companions is still the one who has made a mistake, but he He is Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8057","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-A'la al-Qaysi informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Thawr al-San'ani narrated to us, from Ma'mar ibn Abi 'Amr al-Azdi, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Kathir ibn Kathir ibn al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wada'ah — one of them adding upon the other — from Sa'ib ibn Jubayr al-Asadi, who said: Ibn 'Abbas said:\n\n\"The first woman to adopt the minṭaq (waist belt/girdle) was the mother of Isma'il. She took a minṭaq so as to conceal her trace from Sarah. Then Ibrahim came with her and her son Isma'il while she was nursing him, until he placed her near the House. At that time there was no one in Makkah, nor was there any water there. He placed her there, and placed with her a leather bag containing dates and a water-skin containing water. Then Ibrahim turned to depart, and the mother of Isma'il followed him. She said: 'O Ibrahim, where are you going, leaving us in this valley where there is no companion and nothing at all?' She said this to him repeatedly, but he would not turn to her. Then she said: 'Has Allah commanded you to do this?' He said: 'Yes.' She said: 'Then He will not abandon us.' Then she returned.\n\nIbrahim set out, directing his face toward the House. Then he raised his hands and made these supplications, saying: 'I have settled some of your offspring in a barren valley near Your Sacred House…' until His words: 'that they may give thanks.' The mother of Isma'il continued to nurse Isma'il and drink from that water, until what was in the water-skin was exhausted. She became thirsty, her son became thirsty, and he grew hungry. She set out, not wishing to look at him. She found al-Safa to be the nearest mountain to her. She stood upon it, faced the valley, and looked — did she see anyone? She saw no one. She descended from al-Safa until, when she reached the valley, she raised the hem of her garment. Then she ran with the exertion of one struggling. Then she came to al-Marwa. She stood upon it and looked — did she see anyone? She saw no one. She did this seven times.\n\nIbn 'Abbas said: The Prophet ﷺ said: 'For this reason the people run between them (al-Safa and al-Marwa).'\n\nWhen she came down from al-Marwa, she heard a sound. She said: 'Silence!' — meaning to herself. She listened again and heard it once more. She said: 'I have indeed heard you — if you have any relief (to offer).' And there she was, at the angel's location at the place of Zamzam, striking with his heel or his wing, until the water appeared. She came, shaping it with her hands, as it were, and she began to scoop water from it into her water-skin, and it gushed forth in proportion to what she scooped.\n\nIbn 'Abbas said: The Prophet ﷺ said: 'May Allah have mercy on the mother of Isma'il. Had she left Zamzam' — or he said: 'Had she not scooped from the water' — 'it would have been a flowing spring.' She drank and nursed her child. The angel said: 'Do not fear abandonment, for here is the House of Allah, which this boy and his father shall build. And Allah does not abandon His people.'\n\nThe House was elevated from the ground like a mound, with torrents flowing to its right and to its left. They remained in this state until a party — or he said: a household — from Jurhum passed by. They encamped in the lower part of Makkah. They saw a bird hovering and said: 'This bird must be circling over water, though we know of no water in this valley.' They sent a scout, and lo, they found the water. They returned and informed them of the water. The mother of Isma'il was at the water. They said: 'Will you permit us to settle with you?' She said: 'Yes, but you have no right over the water.'\n\nIbn 'Abbas said: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: 'The mother of Isma'il, who loved company, found that (agreeable).' So they settled, and they sent for their families, and they came down with them. The boy grew up and learned Arabic from them, and they admired him when he grew. When he reached maturity, they married him a woman from among them. Then the mother of Isma'il passed away.\""
"8058","Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak informed us, saying: Abu 'Amir and 'Uthman ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Nafi', from Kathir ibn Kathir, from Sa'ib ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said:\n\n\"When there occurred between the people of Ibrahim and his family what occurred, he went out, along with Isma'il and the mother of Isma'il, and with them was a water-skin containing water. She would drink the water and her milk would flow upon her child. When they entered Makkah, he placed her beneath a large tree. Then he turned back, and the mother of Isma'il followed his tracks until she reached Kuday. She called out to him: 'O Ibrahim, to whom are you leaving us?' Abu 'Amir said: 'To whom are you entrusting us?' He said: 'To Allah, the Almighty, the Majestic.' She said: 'I am content with Allah.' Then she returned. She continued to drink from it, and her milk flowed upon her child. When it was exhausted and thirst afflicted the child, she said: 'Were I to go and look, perhaps I might sense someone.' She stood upon al-Safa, but she sensed no one. She descended, and when she reached the valley, she raised her garment. Then she ran until she came to al-Marwa. She looked but sensed no one. She did this several rounds. Then she said: 'Were I only to look over and see what he has done.' And there he was, in his state. But her soul refused until she returned, perhaps she would sense someone. She did this until she completed seven rounds. Then she said: 'Were I only to look over and see what he has done.' And there he was, in his state. And lo, she heard a sound. She said: 'I have heard — speak, and you will be answered, or good shall come to you from your side.'\n\nAbu 'Amir said: She had indeed heard, and lo, it was Jibril. He struck with his foot and the water gushed forth. The mother of Isma'il went digging. Abu al-Qasim ﷺ said: 'Had the mother of Isma'il left the water, it would have been visible (flowing on the surface).'\n\nA group from Jurhum passed by and saw the bird. They said: 'This bird can only be over water.' They sent their messenger and their scout. They came to her and said: 'May we not be with you?' She said: 'Yes.' So they settled with her. Isma'il ﷺ married a woman from among them.\n\nThen it occurred to Ibrahim ﷺ. He said: 'I wish to look upon those I have left behind.' He came and asked about Isma'il: 'Where is he?' They said: 'He is hunting.' They offered him nothing. He said: 'When he comes, tell him: Change the threshold of your door.' He came and she informed him. He said: 'You are that (one).' So return to your family.'\n\nThen it occurred to Ibrahim ﷺ. He said: 'I wish to look upon those I have left behind.' He came to the family of Isma'il and said: 'Where is he?' They said: 'He has gone hunting.' They said to him: 'Dine and drink.' He said: 'What is your food and your drink?' They said: 'Our food is meat and our drink is water.' He said: 'O Allah, bless them in their food and their drink.'\n\nAbu al-Qasim ﷺ said: 'Blessing has not ceased in it due to the supplication of Ibrahim ﷺ.'\n\nThen it occurred to Ibrahim ﷺ. He said: 'I wish to look upon those I have left behind.' He came, and there was Isma'il ﷺ behind Zamzam, fixing his arrows. He said: 'O Isma'il, my Lord, the Almighty, the Majestic, has commanded me to build a House for Him.' He said: 'Obey your Lord.' He said: 'And He has commanded me that you assist me in it.' He said: 'So Isma'il ﷺ began handing Ibrahim the stones, and the two of them were saying: Our Lord, accept from us; indeed You are the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.' When the building was raised and the old man grew weak to lift the stones, he stood upon the Maqam. Isma'il began handing him the stones, and the two of them were saying: Our Lord, accept from us; indeed You are the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.\""
"8059","8106 Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr told us, and he is Ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Musa On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The superiority of Aisha over women is like the superiority of porridge over all other foods.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8060","8107 Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Shazan told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Umm Salamah, do not trouble me about Aisha, for by God the revelation has not come to me in “The quilt of any woman among you, except her.”"
"8061","8108 Muhammad bin Adam bin Sulayman informed us, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Salih bin Rabi’ah bin Hudayr, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “An inspiration was sent to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while I was with him, so I got up and opened the door. When he turned it away from him, he said: O Aisha, indeed Gabriel greets you with peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8062","8109 Ali bin Al-Hussein and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna informed us. They said: I am Khalid. He said: I am Praiseworthy. Anas said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. He said: “I entered Paradise, and I heard a whispering before my hands, and suddenly I saw Al-Ghumaysa’a, the daughter of Milhan. Humaid said: She is Umm Sulaym.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8063","8110 Nusayr bin Al-Faraj told us, he said: I am Shuaib bin Harb, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah bin Abi Salamah, he said: I am Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was shown that I had been admitted to Paradise, so when I In Al-Rumaysa, the wife of Abu Talha, the mother of Sulaym.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8064","8111 Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah informed us, saying: My father told me, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik said: “Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by Umm Sulaym, he would enter and greet her.”"
"8065","8112 Amr bin Mansour informed us. He said: I am Abdullah bin Abdul Wahhab. He said: I am Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad. He said: He informed me. Ibrahim bin Uqba, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Sisters are believers: Maymunah’s husband The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith, Salma the wife of Hamza, and Asma bint Umays, their maternal sisters.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8066","8113 Abdah bin Abdullah informed us, he said: I am Yahya, he is the son of Adam. He said: I am Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: “My brother and I came from Yemen to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So we stayed for a while, and we did not think that Ibn Masoud and his mother were anything but from the house of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, due to the large number of their visitors. And their adherence to Him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8067","8114 Musa bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: I am Abu Usama, he said: Burayd told me, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: “ Asma bint Umays visited Hafsa, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she had migrated to the Negus, among those who migrated to him. So Omar went to see Hafsa, and Asma was with her. When Omar saw Asma, he said: Who is this? She said: Asma bint Umays. Omar said: This Ethiopian, or this Bahariya? Asma said: Yes, then Omar said: We preceded you in the migration, so we have more right to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Ali, may God bless him and grant him peace. She became angry and said: No, by God. You were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, feeding your hungry and advising. Ignorant of you, and we were in a home, or in the hated and hostile land of Abyssinia, and that is in the Book of God, and in His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, By God, I will not eat food or drink anything until I mention what I said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. We were being harmed and afraid. So I will mention that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and by God, I will not lie or add to that. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, She said: O Prophet of God, Omar said: Such and such. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What did you say? She said: I said: So and so. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He has no more right to me than you. He and his companions have one migration, and you and the people of the ship have two migrations. She said: I saw Abu Musa, may God be pleased with him, and the ship’s owners coming to me in messengers, asking about this hadith. There is nothing in this world. I am more happy and there is nothing greater in their souls than what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them. Abu Burdah said. Asmaa said: I saw Abu Musa, and this hadith will not be repeated from me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8068","8115 Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman informed us, saying: I heard Shuaib bin Al-Layth, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Bakr bin Sawadah, On the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, “Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, married Asma’ Bint Umays, after Ja`far ibn Abi Talib, so he went to Asma, and when he left to sit in his house, he found himself in trouble, so he returned. To the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he informed him. Abu Bakr said: What is that if I saw evil? Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: God Almighty exonerated her from that, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and said: No man should enter while he is absent unless someone else is with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8069","8116 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, meaning Ibn Mahdi, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, He said: I heard Habat al-Arni. He said: I heard Ali saying: “I was the first to pray with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8070","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murrah, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam said: “The first to pray with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Ali.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8071","8118 Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, said: “The first to convert to Islam with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Ali bin Abi Talib.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8072","Abdullah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ibn Idris told us, he said: I heard Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam said: “The first to greet Ali”"
"8073","Ismail bin Masoud told us, on the authority of Khaled, who is Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, he said: I heard Abu Hamza, the client of the Ansar, said: I heard Zaid bin Arqam saying: “The first to pray with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Ali,” and he said In another place: Ali greeted me."
"8074","Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Muhammad al-Kufi told me, saying: Sa`id bin Khuthaym told us, on the authority of Asad bin Abdullah al-Bajli, on the authority of Yahya bin Afif, on the authority of Afif, he said: “In pre-Islamic times, I came to Mecca, and descended upon Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, and when the sun rose and set In the sky, while I was looking at the Kaaba, a young man approached and cast his gaze to the sky, then he faced the Qiblah, and the one facing it stood up and did not He waited until a boy came and stood to his right. He did not wait until a woman came and stood behind them. The young man kneeled, and the boy kneeled. And the woman, so the young man rose, so the boy and the woman rose, so the young man fell down, prostrating, and he prostrated with him, so I said: O Abbas, this is a great matter, and he said to me: A great matter? He said: Do you know who this young man is? I said: No. He said: This is Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Muttalib. This is my nephew. He said: Do you know who this boy is? I said: No. He said: Ali bin Abi Talib bin Abdul Muttalib. This is my nephew. Do you know who this is? The woman behind them? I said: No. He said: This is Khadija, the daughter of Khuwaylid, the wife of this nephew of mine. Tell me that your Lord is the Lord of the heavens. And the earth is his command according to this religion which he follows, and by God there is no one on the face of the entire earth who follows this religion except these three.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8075","8122 Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: Al-Ala’ bin Salih told us, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, On the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah, he said: Ali said: “I am the servant of God, and the brother of His Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I am the greatest friend, no He says it after me except a liar. I prayed seven years before the people.”"
"8076","8123 Ali bin Al-Mundhir told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, he said: Al-Ajlah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Hudhayl, on the authority of Ali, he said: “I do not know of anyone from this nation who worshiped God after its Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, except me. I worshiped God before he worshiped Him.” anyone of this nation for seven years.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8077","8124 Hilal bin Bishr told me, he said: Muhammad bin Khaled, who is Ibn Uthma, told us, he said: Musa bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Muhajir bin Mismar told me, on the authority of Aisha bint Saad, who said: I heard my father saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day Al-Juhfah and took Ali’s hand and delivered a speech, thanking God and praising Him, then he said: O people, I am your guardian. They said: You are right, O Messenger of God, then he took Ali’s hand and raised it, and said: This is my guardian, and the one who will perform on my behalf, and God is loyal to whoever is loyal to him, and hostile to whoever is hostile to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8078","8125 Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Al-Hasan bin Hammad told us, he said: Musahar bin Abdul-Malik told us, on the authority of Issa bin Omar, On the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had a bird with him, and he said: “O God, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You. He was eating with me some of this bird, so Abu Bakr came and sent it away, Omar came and sent it away, and Ali came and gave him permission.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8079","8126 Qutaibah bin Saeed and Hisham bin Ammar told us, saying: Hatim told us, on the authority of Bukayr bin Mismar, on the authority of Aamir bin Saad bin Abu Waqqas, he said: “Muawiyah ordered Sa’d and said: What prevented you from cursing Abu Turab?” He said: As for what I mentioned three things that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about them. May God bless him and grant him peace, I will not curse him, because I have one of them more beloved to me than red camels. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said to him, and he succeeded him in some of his battles, so Ali said to him: O Messenger of God, do you leave me behind with the women and children? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him May God bless him and grant him peace: Aren’t you satisfied to be to me what Aaron was to Moses, except that there will be no prophethood after me? And I heard him say on the Day of Khaybar: I will give the banner to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and God and His Messenger love him. So we debated over it, and he said: Call upon Ali for me, and he was brought to Armad. So he spit in his eyes, and pushed the banner to him, and when it came down, Hisham added: God only desires to remove the uncleanness from you, O People of the House. He called The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted Ali, Fatima, Hassan, and Husayn, and he said: Oh God, I mean these are my family. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8080","Harami bin Yunus bin Muhammad told us, he said: Abu Ghassan told us, he said: Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Musa al-Saghir, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Sabit, on the authority of Saad Ibn Abi Waqqas, who said: “I was sitting, and they targeted Ali Ibn Abi Talib, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said he has three qualities, because having one of them is dearer to me than red camels. I heard him say: He is in the same position as me. Aaron is from Moses, except that there is no prophet after me, and I heard him say: Tomorrow I will give the banner to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and God loves him. And His Messenger, and I heard him say: Whoever I am his master, then Ali is his master.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8081","8128 Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Nasr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdullah bin Dawud informed us, on the authority of Abdul Wahid Bin Ayman, on the authority of his father, that Saad said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Tomorrow I will hand over the banner to a man who loves God and His Messenger. And God and His Messenger love him, and God will grant him victory, so his companions looked forward to her, so he handed her over to Ali.”"
"8082","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Ibn Abi Laila told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of his father, that he said to Ali, who was walking with him: “The people disapproved of you because you went out in the cold in The two sheets, and going out in the heat in the padding, and the thick dress. He said: Were you not with us in Khaybar? He said: Yes, he said: Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. God, peace and blessings be upon him, sent Abu Bakr and appointed a banner for him, so he returned. He sent Omar and appointed a banner for him, and he returned with the people, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: I will give the banner to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and is not a fugitive. So he sent for me, and I was turning a blind eye. I said: I am turning a blind eye, so he spit on me. My eyes, and said: Oh God, protect him from the harm of heat and cold, for I did not find any heat or cold after that.”"
"8083","8130 Muhammad bin Ali bin Harb Al-Maruzi informed us, saying: Muadh bin Khalid informed us, saying: Al-Hussein bin Waqid informed us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, said: I heard Buraidah, saying: “We besieged Khaybar, and he took the general Abu Bakr and did not open for him, and he took from Tomorrow Omar came, so he left and it was not opened for him, and the people were beset that day with distress and effort, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I am defending My banner tomorrow will go to a man who loves God and His Messenger, and God and His Messenger love him. He will not return until it is opened for him, and we will sleep peacefully, because The conquest was held tomorrow, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the morning prayer, then he stood up and called for the banner, while the people were in their ranks, and what “There is a person among us who has a status with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except for him, who hopes to be the bearer of the standard.” So he called Ali bin Abi Talib And he was gray-haired, so he spit in his eyes, wiped it off, and the banner was given to him, and God granted victory to him. He said: “And I am among those who treated her badly.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8084","8131 Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Awf told us, on the authority of Maimun Abi Abdullah, that Abdul Allah bin Buraidah told him, on the authority of Buraidah Al-Aslami, he said: “When he was staying where the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, resided in the presence of the people of Khaybar, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave the general to Omar, and some of the people rose with him and met the people of Khaybar, and Omar and his companions were revealed. So they returned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I will give the banner to a man who loves God and His Messenger. And God and His Messenger love him. So the next day, Abu Bakr and Omar went out and called for Ali, who was gray-haired. He spit in his eyes and got up. With him were some people who got up and met the people of Khaybar. Suddenly, Marhab was shaking and saying: Khaybar has learned that I am welcome. He who wields weapons is a proven hero. Sometimes I stab and sometimes I strike, when the lions approached, flaming, so he and Ali struck each other twice, and Ali struck him on the head until he was bitten. The tip of the sword turned white, and the people of the army heard the sound of its strike. The last of the people had not finished with Ali before God granted victory for him and for them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"8085","8132 Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, he said: Sahl bin Sa’d told me, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He said on the Day of Khaybar: “Tomorrow I will give this banner to a man upon whom God will give victory, who loves God and His Messenger, and whom God will love.” And His Messenger. When the morning came, the people went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, all of them hoping to be given something. He said: Where is Ali bin Abi Talib? They said: O Messenger of God, his eyes are complaining. He said: So they sent for him, and he was brought. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spit in his eye. He prayed for him, and he was healed, as if he had no ailment, so he gave him the standard. Ali said: O Messenger of God, will I fight them until they are like us? : Follow your messengers until you land in their square, then invite them to Islam, and inform them of what is required of them by God, for by God For God to guide one man through you is better for you than to have red camels.”"
